        "origin": "fact",
        "source": {
          "file": "workspace/large-n-proof.qmd"
        },
        "statement": "There are universal constants $S_0,C>0$ such that, for normalized conformal data from @def-conformal-data with $S\\le S_0$, if $v$ is the positive first solution of\n$$\n-\\Delta v=\\lambda|1+g|^2v\\quad\\text{in }\\mathbb D,qquad v|_{\\partial\\mathbb D}=0,qquad \\int_{\\mathbb D}v^2|1+g|^2=1,\n$$\nthen, with $J$ as in @def-j-functional,\n$$\n\\frac{J(P)}{\\pi j^2}=1+S-\\sum_{n\\ge2}\\frac{\\rho_n}{(n+1)^2}|g_n|^2+R(g),qquad |R(g)|\\le CS^{3/2},\n$$\nwhere $\\rho_n=jJ_{n+1}(j)/J_n(j)$ and $0<\\rho_n<2$. In particular,\n$$\n\\frac{J(P)}{\\pi j^2}-1\\ge S/6.\n$$",
        "title": "Uniform disk perturbation expansion"
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-edge-moments",
        "identity": {
          "statement_hash": "sha256:9fe8d6f1f823d7f899ec056bada7582af5281fd0da8b88781d7c08b1b8a825dd"
