      "origin": "fact",
      "identity": {
        "statement_hash": "sha256:37405282ce04c69408d1eb59b3e1fbf43953d02870323c51e9ed9b878d590dc6"
      },
      "source": {
        "file": "workspace/large-n-proof.qmd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "def-j-functional",
      "kind": "definition",
      "title": "Area-eigenvalue functional",
      "statement": "For an admissible polygon $P$ in @def-admissible-polygon, let $\\lambda_1(P)$ be the first Dirichlet eigenvalue of $-\\Delta$ on the bounded nondegenerate polygonal domain $P$ and define\n$$\nJ(P)=A(P)\\lambda_1(P),\\qquad\nm_k=\\inf\\{J(Q):Q\\text{ is admissible and has at most }k\\text{ effective edges}\\}.\n$$\nHere $k\\ge3$ is an integer, and $R_k$ denotes the unit-area regular $k$-gon (its position is irrelevant because $J$ is similarity invariant). The first eigenvalue is defined by the Dirichlet Rayleigh quotient on $H_0^1(P)$.",
      "origin": "fact",
      "identity": {
        "statement_hash": "sha256:53054b04c549c94bda17d3823792506093e3009a788d21ff01ca9a7fad6d7724"
      },
      "source": {
        "file": "workspace/large-n-proof.qmd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "def-turn-measure",
      "kind": "definition",
      "title": "Signed Schwarz-Christoffel turn measure",
      "statement": "At the prevertices $e^{i\\theta_i}$ of an admissible polygon in @def-admissible-polygon, with normalized conformal map from @def-conformal-data, put\n$$\nw_i=\\frac{\\pi-\\omega_i}{2\\pi},\\qquad\n\\mu=\\sum_iw_i\\delta_{\\theta_i},\\qquad \\widehat\\mu(n)=\\int e^{-in\\theta}d\\mu(\\theta).\n$$\nThen $\\sum_iw_i=1$ and $\\widehat\\mu(1)=0$ in the chosen $F''(0)=0$ normalization. The Schwarz--Christoffel derivative has logarithm\n$$\nL(z)=\\log F'(z)=2\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\frac{\\widehat\\mu(n)}n z^n,\n$$\nso $L_n=2\\widehat\\mu(n)/n$. This definition applies to finite real atomic measures induced by such polygons; all Fourier series below are interpreted in that class.",
      "origin": "fact",
      "identity": {
        "statement_hash": "sha256:c2f418b6da528c0ee3b88a5bb0f9f4f6c75fd3b52b693f26274bcf2526c3d135"
      },
      "source": {
        "file": "workspace/large-n-proof.qmd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-atom-deletion",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "title": "Deletion preserves the comparison energy",
      "statement": "Let $(P_N)$ be a sequence of stationary admissible $N$-gons with effective-edge canonical presentations, satisfying @lem-edge-moments, @lem-disk-perturbation, @lem-gradient-perturbation, @lem-spectral-core, @lem-near-circle-conformal, and $J(P_N)\\le J(R_{N-1})$, in the one-reflex regime of @def-turn-measure. Let $p=N-1$, let $a$ be the small positive atom from @lem-single-reflex-small-atom, and define $E_b$ as in @def-positive-kernel. Put\n$$\n\\widetilde\\mu=\\frac{\\mu-a\\delta_{\\theta_*}}{1-a}.\n$$\nThen $\\widetilde\\mu$ has total mass $1$ and $N-2$ positive atoms, and\n$$\nE_b(\\widetilde\\mu)-E_b(\\mu)=o(N^{-4}).\n$$",
      "origin": "fact",
      "identity": {
        "statement_hash": "sha256:4372825ae31c0dbf2d9738d41a91dcf642a2b29b95d8ba5b6a8d497d554ca54d"
      },
      "source": {
        "file": "workspace/large-n-proof.qmd"
      }
