      "source": {
        "file": "workspace/large-n-proof.qmd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-disk-perturbation",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "title": "Uniform disk perturbation expansion",
      "statement": "There are universal constants $S_0,C>0$ such that, for normalized conformal data from @def-conformal-data with $S\\le S_0$, if $v$ is the positive first solution of\n$$\n-\\Delta v=\\lambda|1+g|^2v\\quad\\text{in }\\mathbb D,qquad v|_{\\partial\\mathbb D}=0,qquad \\int_{\\mathbb D}v^2|1+g|^2=1,\n$$\nthen, with $J$ as in @def-j-functional,\n$$\n\\frac{J(P)}{\\pi j^2}=1+S-\\sum_{n\\ge2}\\frac{\\rho_n}{(n+1)^2}|g_n|^2+R(g),qquad |R(g)|\\le CS^{3/2},\n$$\nwhere $j=j_{0,1}$ is the first positive zero of $J_0$, $\\rho_n=jJ_{n+1}(j)/J_n(j)$, and $0<\\rho_n<2$. In particular,\n$$\n\\frac{J(P)}{\\pi j^2}-1\\ge S/6.\n$$\nMoreover, writing $g=t h$ with $t=\\sqrt S$ and $\\|h\\|_{A^2}=1$, the corresponding normalized eigenpair satisfies\n$$\n\\|v-v_0\\|_{H^1_0(\\mathbb D)}\\le Ct,\n\\qquad |\\lambda-j^2|\\le Ct^2.\n$$",
      "origin": "fact",
      "identity": {
        "statement_hash": "sha256:ca3b650d7594209db8a0019259f09ca81ed4e37cf349188bc633c73916e83c80"
      },
      "source": {
        "file": "workspace/large-n-proof.qmd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-edge-moments",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "title": "Stationary edge moments",
      "statement": "Let $P$ be admissible and stationary in the sense of @def-stationary-polygon. If $u>0$ is the $L^2$-normalized first eigenfunction, $\\lambda=\\lambda_1(P)$, $c=\\lambda/A(P)$, and $q=|\\partial_\\nu u|^2$, then every effective edge $E$, parametrized by physical arclength $s\\in[0,\\ell_E]$, satisfies\n$$\n\\int_E(q-c)\\,ds=0,\\qquad \\int_Es(q-c)\\,ds=0.\n$$",
      "origin": "fact",
      "identity": {
        "statement_hash": "sha256:9fe8d6f1f823d7f899ec056bada7582af5281fd0da8b88781d7c08b1b8a825dd"
      },
