    {
      "id": "lem-single-reflex-small-atom",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "title": "Single-reflex small positive atom",
      "statement": "There is a universal $C$ such that a stationary admissible $N$-gon with an effective-edge canonical presentation, satisfying @lem-edge-moments, @lem-disk-perturbation, and $J(P)\\le J(R_{N-1})$ in the regime of @lem-near-circle-conformal, with exactly one reflex corner, has an adjacent convex corner $i$ whose turn weight $a=w_i>0$ in @def-turn-measure satisfies\n$$\na\\le C N^{-9/4}\\sqrt{\\log N}.\n$$",
      "origin": "fact",
      "identity": {
