    {
      "id": "lem-spectral-core",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "title": "Uniform nonlinear spectral lower bound",
      "statement": "There are universal constants $C$ and $S_0>0$ such that every stationary polygon whose canonical boundary presentation consists entirely of effective edges, satisfying @lem-edge-moments, @lem-disk-perturbation, and @lem-gradient-perturbation, and lying in the regime of @lem-near-circle-conformal, with $S\\le S_0$, satisfies\n$$\n\\frac{J(P)}{\\pi j^2}\\ge 1+4\\sum_{n\\ge2}a_n|\\widehat\\mu(n)|^2-C S^{3/2}\\sqrt{\\log(e/S)},\n$$\nwhere @def-turn-measure defines $\\mu$ and\n$$\na_n=\\frac{\\beta_n}{n^2(n+1)^2}\\left(1+\\frac{\\beta_n}{n^2-1}\\right),\n\\qquad \\beta_n=n+1-j\\frac{J_{n+1}(j)}{J_n(j)}.\n$$",
